      "role": "user",
      "content": "but the blisters arent even popping yet so its not an open wound... it's just the skin feeling really hot and angry. and i read in a wellness blog that the fats in butter or even coconut oil actually create a protective barrier that helps the skin regenerate faster by locking in moisture. if i just do a thick layer of oil or butter now, wouldn't that basically act like a natural bandage and stop the heat from going deeper into my arm? it feels much safer than some doctor applying potentially harsh chemicals to it.",
